WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:01.859
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:01.859 --> 00:00:04.710
That number is two one nine two David P..

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.610
Here is a fair question about Joe Biden.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.599
And it sort of relates to our conversation
earlier.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:11.759
Let's take a listen to it.

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:17.400
David, I just want to know, what were your
main critiques of Biden policy?

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:28.580
I just wanted to know the guy into the 2020
election knowing, like, what do you disagree

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.930
with him on?

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.289
Thank you, God.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.289
OK.

00:00:32.289 --> 00:00:36.470
So listen, there is no way to sum this up
in one segment, but every time I've done an

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:42.360
analysis of a Joe Biden proposal, Joe Biden's
health care proposal, Joe Biden's tax plan.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:48.410
Joe Biden on climate or whatever else, I will
point out where he falls short.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.990
And I think what's important here is context.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:55.170
So, for example, Joe Biden's tax plan is actually
quite solid and a lot of very good things

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.170
in it.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:59.190
It doesn't, for example, create new higher
tax brackets.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.830
I think we need right now the highest tax
bracket, I think is around five hundred and

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:03.830
fifty thousand dollars.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.910
We probably need tax brackets like at the
one point five or two million dollar level.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.670
Five or 10 million.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.670
Fifteen hundred.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.620
You know, but we need higher levels and higher
tax rates at those higher levels.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.190
He doesn't do that.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.159
That's a critique of Joe Biden's tax plan.

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:21.980
And Joe Biden's tax plan does a lot of good
things.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:26.700
When we looked at Joe Biden's clean energy
and climate change plan, it does many good

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:33.190
things, but it fell short in some areas in
terms of certain requirements, pollution requirements.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:38.880
As you know, I outlined them in that clip
when we've talked about Joe Biden on health

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:39.880
care.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.640
Joe Biden's plan will give way more people
access to health care and it will make health

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.890
care affordable for way more people.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.890
But it's not going to be comprehensive and
universal.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:49.890
As an example.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:55.100
So with all of these questions, the reason
I'm doing this is that's it feels to me that

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.770
that voicemail was a good faith question.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:01.790
It was not a question meant to do this stuff
of if it's not Bernie, then who cares if it's

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:02.790
Trump?

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:06.729
It seems like it's just I'm curious, where
do you disagree with Joe Biden?

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.250
And I disagree with Joe Biden in many areas.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:15.680
And yet the reality that I must vote for Joe
Biden is not missed at any point in time.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.260
And it is abundantly and completely clear.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.749
And my critiques of Joe Biden have not been
done in a way to even remotely suggest maybe

00:02:23.749 --> 00:02:25.859
we stay home or vote for Trump.

00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:29.370
Joe Biden's plans don't do everything that
we want them to do.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.650
Taking the Senate in November, in addition
to winning the White House, would best enable

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:38.499
us to have two straight years, two solid years
during which we can push the Senate and the

00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:42.790
House and Joe Biden to pass as much progressive
change as possible.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.730
And that's all we can really say right now.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:49.900
And so my goal from here on out is I have
no problem critiquing Joe Biden's policy where

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.950
it falls short and that's what I do.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:55.219
If I wasn't doing that, I really would be
doing you a disservice.

00:02:55.219 --> 00:03:00.140
But I'm not going to do it in a way that might
leave anybody thinking, whoa, is David sort

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.909
of saying maybe we don't vote for by now?

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:02.909
I'm not going to do that.

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:06.480
It's going to be made clear in every single
segment that that's what has to happen.

